//
// New York: New York State income tax, plus the New York City resident tax
// and the Yonkers resident surcharge, which NY employers withhold for
// residents of those cities.
//
// Method: NY's Method II (exact calculation), with each pay frequency's own
// table, and Method III (top income rates) once annualized net wages reach
// the booklet's threshold. The arithmetic follows the booklets' worked
// examples step for step, including rounding the Step 4 product to the cent.
//
// Tables were generated by tools/state/generate_ny.py from the NY Tax
// Department's 2026 booklets (NYS-50-T-NYS, NYS-50-T-NYC, NYS-50-T-Y), not
// typed by hand. The generator checks every published Table A allowance
// against Table B + N x Table C. The Yonkers booklet's tables are identical
// to the State's (checked when generating), so the Yonkers resident
// surcharge is the State amount x 16.75%, exactly as NYS-50-T-Y says.
// Rows are [atLeastCents, rateTenThousandths, plusCents]: 0.0753 -> 753.
//
// Wages: NY withholds on 401(k) deferrals only if they're subject to
// federal income tax withholding (NYS-50, Part E and the taxability table),
// so the base is federal income-tax wages.
//
// IT-2104 input: { filingStatus: "single" | "married" | "marriedAtSingleRate",
//   stateAllowances (line 1, also used for Yonkers), nycAllowances (line 2),
//   nycResident, yonkersResident, worksInYonkers (employer-set; see the
//   nonresident earnings tax below), additionalStateCents (line 3),
//   additionalNycCents (line 4), additionalYonkersCents (line 5) }.
// "single" covers head of household (IT-2104: mark Single or Head of household).
//
// No IT-2104 on file: zero allowances (NYS-50 and IT-2104 instructions). If
// the employee's federal W-4 is from 2019 or earlier, NY lets the employer
// use its allowances and marital status instead, and this does. NY doesn't
// name a filing status for the zero-allowance case; this uses Single, the
// higher-withholding choice, and says so (formBasis). City residency comes
// from the IT-2104, so with no IT-2104 no city tax is withheld.
//
// Yonkers NONRESIDENT earnings tax (NYS-50-T-Y, Method VIII, annualized):
// for an employee who works in Yonkers but doesn't live there - a fact the
// employer knows, so it's an extra form field, `worksInYonkers`. Annualize,
// skip under $4,000, subtract the exclusion for the line ($3,000 to
// $10,000; $2,000 to $20,000; $1,000 to $30,000; none above), x 0.50%,
// divide by the periods. Returned as the YONKERS_NR locality. The booklet's
// example ($400 semimonthly -> $1.38) is in the tests.
//
// Not covered: pay frequencies other than daily, weekly, biweekly,
// semimonthly, monthly and annual.

